The rule as written says the grounding verdict is computed with "no relaxation, value-in-span checked" and returns one of "GROUNDED, SPAN_MISSING, SPAN_NOT_IN_DOCUMENT or VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN". Changing the value from "cat" to "dog" while keeping the same span and document means the value is no longer in the span, so the verdict should move from GROUNDED to VALUE_NOT_IN_SPAN. That is a move.